  "guide": {
    "title": "Follow a request through middleware",
    "introduction": {
      "text": "Middleware functions share one Context. Each function can call next() to enter the next function. This guide follows that call and the return path.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "claim:87cd957c-bb51-49fe-b9a4-291c106e08c5",
        "claim:005c1ad3-dcc5-4f77-b36f-7ee4a420f22c",
        "claim:f67de3f4-647c-4c67-86e3-ab561267bf22"
      ],
      "unknown_indices": []
    },
    "example": {
      "title": "Start with two functions that wait",
      "description": {
        "text": "Assume both middleware functions use await next(), and later work returns normally. The second function resumes before the first. This is an example, not an observed execution.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "claim:87cd957c-bb51-49fe-b9a4-291c106e08c5",
          "claim:005c1ad3-dcc5-4f77-b36f-7ee4a420f22c",
          "claim:f67de3f4-647c-4c67-86e3-ab561267bf22"
        ],
        "unknown_indices": [
          2
        ]
      }
    },
    "sections": [
      {
        "key": "start",
        "title": "First, start a fresh run",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "text": "compose returns a runner. Each runner call creates its own index, sets it to -1, and starts dispatch at index zero.",
            "claim_ids": [
              "claim:a4808f91-eb8a-4a52-aed2-72effb4a139e",
              "claim:b1c5caa4-d40d-4e99-a478-a0483a83437a"
            ],
            "unknown_indices": []
          },
          {
            "text": "Before selecting a handler, dispatch requires its index to be greater than the previous one. A repeated or backward index raises an Error.",
            "claim_ids": [
              "claim:25d1b193-56d5-4ad3-8be1-b7bb1bb30d2b",
              "claim:b35b5c02-3b31-46cd-b1ac-2845ca7d8424"
            ],
            "unknown_indices": []
          }
        ],
        "stage_keys": [
          "start",
          "guard"
        ],
        "code": {
          "evidence_id": "evidence:f0fbf304d7f634b2604843eb1d434ace3bbc1661e737c3fd782fde7d77f7b370",
          "start_line": 21,
          "end_line": 23
        }
      },
      {
        "key": "next",
        "title": "Then, follow next() into the next function",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "text": "dispatch selects the middleware handler and updates context.req.routeIndex. At exactly middleware.length, it can select the supplied outer next callback.",
            "claim_ids": [
              "claim:36389804-ee71-4da7-bbdc-e77cb1d247b1",
              "claim:957e5bca-529c-4b7b-85cd-d3ad15c57993",
              "claim:0df938c1-9773-4d05-84ba-5bcecf66fb6c"
            ],
            "unknown_indices": []
          },
          {
            "text": "The callback passed to the handler calls dispatch(i + 1). It uses the same context, so later work can update shared response state.",
            "claim_ids": [
              "claim:87cd957c-bb51-49fe-b9a4-291c106e08c5",
              "claim:fca39081-cbda-4fe7-8212-cf21fdc9a885"
            ],
            "unknown_indices": []
          },
          {
            "text": "The dispatcher waits for the handler result. If the handler uses await next(), it waits for the child dispatch before continuing.",
            "claim_ids": [
              "claim:87cd957c-bb51-49fe-b9a4-291c106e08c5",
              "claim:005c1ad3-dcc5-4f77-b36f-7ee4a420f22c"
            ],
            "unknown_indices": [
              2
            ]
          }
        ],
        "stage_keys": [
          "call"
        ],
        "code": {
          "evidence_id": "evidence:f0fbf304d7f634b2604843eb1d434ace3bbc1661e737c3fd782fde7d77f7b370",
          "start_line": 51,
          "end_line": 51
        }
      },
      {
        "key": "response",
        "title": "As calls complete, select the response state",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "text": "A truthy result updates context.res only when the context is not finalized or the result came from onError.",
            "claim_ids": [
              "claim:fca39081-cbda-4fe7-8212-cf21fdc9a885"
            ],
            "unknown_indices": []
          },
          {
            "text": "A normal result therefore keeps an already finalized response. A truthy onError result can replace it. A falsy result makes no assignment.",
            "claim_ids": [
              "claim:1724bbd4-e936-42d3-a4cd-dabd7f2051aa",
              "claim:d5e3c85d-4a1d-4991-87d8-bd5369c091ab",
              "claim:7f3aafe6-876f-4b5a-9bac-698144b2adfc"
            ],
            "unknown_indices": []
          },
          {
            "text": "If no handler is selected, onNotFound runs only when finalized is false and the callback exists. A completed dispatch call returns the shared context.",
            "claim_ids": [
              "claim:e8b03c7a-182a-46d4-aeb8-bf4295b82798",
              "claim:f67de3f4-647c-4c67-86e3-ab561267bf22"
            ],
            "unknown_indices": []
          }
        ],
        "stage_keys": [
          "response"
        ],
        "code": {
          "evidence_id": "evidence:f0fbf304d7f634b2604843eb1d434ace3bbc1661e737c3fd782fde7d77f7b370",
          "start_line": 67,
          "end_line": 70
        }
      },
      {
        "key": "errors",
        "title": "If a call fails, check which frame can catch it",
        "paragraphs": [
          {
            "text": "The handler catch invokes onError only for an Error instance when that callback exists. It first stores the Error in context.error.",
            "claim_ids": [
              "claim:544dbd7e-acd1-4040-8b00-00b91c0e8f8d",
              "claim:6a188938-736d-4970-a698-88df4b787329"
            ],
            "unknown_indices": []
          },
          {
            "text": "Other thrown values are rethrown. A failure inside onError also escapes the current catch.",
            "claim_ids": [
              "claim:37cba2c0-333b-4a16-b503-49cd1b020ffa",
              "claim:40001f0b-2785-462a-9244-1997813e69cd"
            ],
            "unknown_indices": []
          },
          {
            "text": "The repeated-next guard and not-found callback are outside the current handler catch block. An awaiting parent may still catch a child failure.",
            "claim_ids": [
              "claim:6b252ce9-9a3f-4cdb-9248-b0e515420829",
              "claim:5a6d5b53-546a-4ad0-bb93-b028876d1d12"
            ],
            "unknown_indices": [
              3
            ]
          }
        ],
        "stage_keys": [
          "failure"
        ],
        "code": {
          "evidence_id": "evidence:f0fbf304d7f634b2604843eb1d434ace3bbc1661e737c3fd782fde7d77f7b370",
          "start_line": 50,
          "end_line": 60
        }
      }
    ],
    "limits": [
      {
        "text": "Each application function chooses whether to pass work onward and wait. These excerpts do not show those choices.",
        "claim_ids": [],
        "unknown_indices": [
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "An error can move back to an earlier function or to the application. What happens there is outside this review.",
        "claim_ids": [],
        "unknown_indices": [
          3
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
